{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-ghost-playback-017-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/GhostRenderTraceTests.cs", "line": 239, "method": "FormatTracePrefix_UsesInvariantKeyValueFields", "category": "T3", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostRenderTrace.cs:1196; drop CultureInfo.InvariantCulture from FormatDouble -> green on an en-culture host (CI ubuntu-latest), red only on the operator's ro-RO box, so the invariance the name claims is host-dependent rather than pinned", "what_it_asserts": "BuildPrefix emits phase=, rec=, recId=, ghostIndex=, currentUT=123.457 and playbackUT=120.250 as dot-decimal key=value tokens.", "why_weak": "The test never switches CurrentCulture, so on an en-culture host (the CI runner) a FormatDouble that dropped CultureInfo.InvariantCulture still renders dots and the test stays green. Per the house rule, a test that claims invariance proves it by pinning a comma-decimal culture.", "proposed_action": "Wrap the call in a de-DE CurrentCulture scope with a try/finally restore, the way GhostPartEventApplyLogTests scopes its culture check, so the InvariantCulture argument at GhostRenderTrace.cs:1196 is actually load-bearing.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-ghost-playback-017-02", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/GhostExtenderTests.cs", "line": 707, "method": "ChooseStrategy_LogsDecision", "category": "T2", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostExtender.cs:54-58; delete the Verbose call in the Orbital arm -> both red, and no production change reds this test without also redding its twin", "what_it_asserts": "ChooseStrategy on a recording with TerminalOrbitBody=Mun and SMA>0 logs a [GhostExtend] line containing Orbital and the body name.", "why_weak": "ChooseStrategy_OrbitalTerminal_ReturnsOrbital (line 45) drives the same branch and makes the identical log assertion plus the return-value assertion this one omits. No production change can red one without redding the other.", "proposed_action": "Delete ChooseStrategy_LogsDecision, or repoint it at a branch whose log line nothing else asserts (the None / null-recording arms at GhostExtender.cs:31 and :86).", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "coverage", "sut": "GhostExtender", "sut_file": "Source/Parsek/GhostExtender.cs", "sut_line": 86, "case_kind": "negative", "proposed_name": "ChooseStrategy_NoData_LogsTheNoneReasonWithTheRecordingId", "sketch": "Build an empty Recording with a known Id and empty Points, call ChooseStrategy, and assert the captured log carries [GhostExtend], None, and the recording id from the rec= field of the step-4 fallthrough line.", "guards": "The None arm's diagnostic is the only signal an operator gets when a ghost silently refuses to extend; nothing currently asserts its recording-id field, so a reformat that drops rec= would ship unnoticed.", "risk": "playback"}
